zagent is an UNOFFICIAL terminal client for the ZCode agent runtime.
It is not affiliated with, authorized, or endorsed by Z.ai. "ZCode" and "Z.ai"
are trademarks of their respective owners.

This repository does NOT redistribute any Z.ai binaries. The runtime is discovered
and driven from the user's own installation (ZCode desktop bundle or zcode-app-cli).

Intended use
- Non-commercial, personal interoperability and research, against your OWN Z.ai
  account and your OWN installed runtime. Do not use it to access accounts,
  credentials, or services you are not authorized to use.
- The MIT license (see LICENSE) governs this source. "Non-commercial" is the
  project's intent, not a license restriction; the MIT terms still apply.

Interoperability and reverse engineering
- To interoperate with the desktop app, this project implements protocol, local
  credential-store, billing/quota and off-peak contracts that were observed from
  the officially installed desktop app on the author's own machine. Some modules
  (e.g. packages/driver/credentials.mjs, quota.mjs, offpeak.mjs) read the user's
  own local credential store and send desktop-compatible identity headers so the
  CLI is accepted by the same endpoints the desktop uses.
- These interoperability features may be inconsistent with Z.ai's Terms of Service.
